**Clarify first.** Ask: add, search, and maybe toggle/delete? Is search case-insensitive and live while typing? Should data persist? Then build step by step, running often.

**State design.** Store only the minimal state: `todos` (array of `{id, text, done}`), `text` (the input), and `query` (the search string). The visible list is *derived* from `todos` and `query`, not stored separately, which avoids sync bugs.

```jsx
import { useState, useMemo } from "react";

export default function App() {
  const [todos, setTodos] = useState([]);
  const [text, setText] = useState("");
  const [query, setQuery] = useState("");

  const add = (e) => {
    e.preventDefault();
    const t = text.trim();
    if (!t) return;
    setTodos((prev) => [...prev, { id: crypto.randomUUID(), text: t, done: false }]);
    setText("");
  };
  const toggle = (id) =>
    setTodos((prev) => prev.map((x) => (x.id === id ? { ...x, done: !x.done } : x)));
  const remove = (id) => setTodos((prev) => prev.filter((x) => x.id !== id));

  const visible = useMemo(
    () => todos.filter((x) => x.text.toLowerCase().includes(query.toLowerCase())),
    [todos, query]
  );

  return (
    <div>
      <form onSubmit={add}>
        <input value={text} onChange={(e) => setText(e.target.value)} placeholder="Add todo" />
        <button type="submit">Add</button>
      </form>
      <input value={query} onChange={(e) => setQuery(e.target.value)} placeholder="Search" />
      <ul>
        {visible.map((x) => (
          <li key={x.id}>
            <span style={{ textDecoration: x.done ? "line-through" : "none" }}
                  onClick={() => toggle(x.id)}>{x.text}</span>
            <button onClick={() => remove(x.id)}>x</button>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </div>
  );
}
```

**Key points to say aloud.** Use stable ids as keys (not array index); use the functional form of `setState` to avoid stale updates; trim input and ignore empty; derive the filtered list; `useMemo` is optional here but fine for large lists. In React Native, swap `div/ul` for `View`/`FlatList` and `input` for `TextInput` with `onChangeText`, and use `keyExtractor`.

**Extensions.** Debounce search, persist to storage, empty-state message, edit item, tests, and accessibility labels.
